==English==
===Phrase===
{{head|en|phrase|head=[[how]] [[do]] [[you]] [[like]] [[them]] [[apple]]s}}?

# {{colloquial|rhetorical question}} directed [[jestingly]] or [[mockingly]] at someone who has received [[surprising]] information, [[ridicule|ridiculing]] the situation
#: ''"Our governor has just vetoed a bill that would offer more money to our schools. '''How do you like them apples'''?"''
# {{colloquial|rhetorical question|Irish|American}} Used after an actual or proposed action with which the listener might be displeased. Also used after refuting an argument.
#: ''"I can't give you a raise now; if I did, this whole company would go bankrupt, and you wouldn't have a job at all. Now '''how do you like them apples'''?"''
In World War I, something called a Stokes gun fired mortars resembling apples with a stick in them, so they were often referred to as Toffee Apples. In the movie Rio Bravo in 1959, a guy tosses a hand grenade and says "How do ya like them apples?"

